🔢 Program 18-Real-Time Application 2: Complex Number Calculator

📌 Description

A Complex Number Calculator is useful in engineering, signal processing, and simulation applications.

The "Complex" class overloads arithmetic operators such as "+", "-", and "*" so that complex numbers can be manipulated using natural mathematical expressions.

For example:

c1 + c2
c1 - c2
c1 * c2

🎯 OOP Concepts Used

- 🔹 Binary operator overloading
- 🔹 Constructor with default arguments
- 🔹 Constant member functions
- 🔹 Encapsulation

💡 Key Point

Operator overloading allows user-defined objects to be used with familiar mathematical operators.
